\item within this language:\\

\item in other languages:\\

\end{enumerate}
\item[* relevant literature/documents:]
\item[\ \ remarks:]\mbox{}
\begin{enumerate}
\item problems:\\
The complex QPs formed by this rule are supposed to function as modifiers to e.
g. adjectival expressions. In combination with 
such a degreemodifier these (measure) 
adjectives such as {\em alto}, {\em 
largo}  are usually not 
explicit in Spanish. 
Thus the generated construction are slightly marked, but not illformed. In 
case of a temporal adjectives however, the occurrence 
of  the adjective should be blocked. 
\item modifications:\\

\end{enumerate}
\end{description}
